---
description: Rules to produce reusable, human-maintainable and readable code in Unity
globs: **/Assets/**/*
alwaysApply: false
---

- Keep it simple, stupid, including not only code but also comments.
- Reuse and extend existing types (e.g. Singleton, managers) before adding new abstractions.
- Avoid unnecessary coupling by passing one big container containing many irrelevant components.
- Avoid a generic class containing all sorts of functionalities for the sake of convenience.
- Avoid duplicated code; use existing configs (e.g: any sorts of `ScriptableObject`) when possible.
- Avoid defensive null checks; let it scream out error when the object should never be null. For C#
  specifics, see "Null Handling" in [`unity/code-editing.mdc`](unity/code-editing.mdc).
